### Findings (worst first) — all four fixed

**1. `data/70/exclusions.json:16` — the west Exit/Entrance vestibule was an unexplained 689‑cell culled pocket** *(pt 214–282 × 516–566, stats centroid (244, 540), mislabelled "near AISLE 21")*
Crop `/tmp/s70_20.png` and the 16× source render show a room holding the store's west **Exit/Entrance** door pair and two **ICE** merchandisers, entirely untinted. Vector check: the inner partition is unbroken — `(332.0,514.9)→(211.8,514.9)` is a **single line item**, plus `x=211.8 y=514.9‑567.5`, `x=271.5 y=515.1‑539.6` stepping to `x=283.2 y=539.6‑567.6`, all width 0.966. The guide erases walls for doorways with white rects (`[225.9,566.2,256.6,567.9]` at this door, `[347.0,566.5,377.7,568.1]` at the second SW door) — **there is no white rect and no door arc anywhere on the inner partition**. Truth: the drawing seals it, so it is not shopping floor here (zero product labels, aisle badges or department names over ~35 m²); but a 689‑cell pocket must be *stated*. Fix type: **exclusion** traced to the stroke faces (`[[213,516],[270,516],[270,540.5],[282,540.5],[282,566],[213,566]]`) + `walk_truth` must_not `(247,552)` + must `(240,508)` proving the sales floor north of the partition stays open. Free‑cell count is **56558 before and after** — zero shopping floor removed.
⚠️ *Human note recorded in the exclusion:* the real store's inner doors are simply absent from this 2018 schematic. Routing shoppers through the west door would need a door‑punch in `router/`, not a data edit — I did not attempt it. The store still enters via the second SW door (`ENTRANCE 362.6,580.3`).

**2. `data/70/walk_truth.json:38` — unexplained 160‑cell pocket at (934, 218)**
It is the interior of an 8‑pt **white‑filled band** drawn along the NE exterior wall, `(898.8,249.8)-(904.5,255.5)-(971.3,189.1)-(965.4,183.2)` — wall‑thickness artwork behind the Market wall run, not floor (`/tmp/ne_src.png`). Correctly sealed, but undocumented. Fix type: **walk_truth must_not** `(934,218)`.

**3. `data/70/walk_truth.json:20` — no must point at the real Seafood service‑case frontage**
The only Seafood point, `(974,364)`, is the printed title out on the open Market floor (what `inclusions.json` rescues) — **4.7 m east** of the case. The case is the scalloped run `[913.4,341.7,920.5,429.4]` on the Bakery's east wall; its customer face at x≈921‑928 had no coverage. Fix type: **walk_truth must** `(930,400)`.

**4. `data/70/walk_truth.json:21` — no must point on the south front walkway**
The Business Center / Tobacco counter frontage (y≈555‑566, x 480‑740) sat between `(362,563)` and `(728,518)` with nothing in it. Fix type: **walk_truth must** `(600,560)`.

